        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "## Presenter script (policies rotate every 120 s; pin one with the control API)\n\n**Control API:** `curl -X POST 'http://localhost:9100/policy?policy=<name>&auto=off'` \u00b7 re-enable rotation with `?auto=on` \u00b7 vertical purple markers on every panel = policy transitions (hover for details)\n\n| Phase | Say | Watch |\n|-------|-----|-------|\n| **open** | \"NGINX only observes: per-tool, per-client, per-server metrics from parsed MCP traffic \u2014 no enforcement.\" | No dashed lines; 429s at zero; flaky error ratio ~15-20%. |\n| **protect-upstreams** | \"Now NGINX protects backends: allowed rate follows the error ratio \u2014 AIMD, like TCP congestion control.\" | mcp-flaky's dashed limit staircases down to the floor; upstream_limit 429s appear; other upstreams stay at 200. |\n| **fair-clients** | \"Now clients are kept fair: caps derive from average demand, recomputed every second.\" | One shared dashed cap appears; client-purple (top tool caller) clipped; client_limit 429s; others untouched. |\n| **full-control** | \"Everything on, plus routing: unhealthy backends lose *new* sessions \u2014 existing sessions stay pinned (MCP sessions are server-bound).\" | Reroutes/s fire flaky\u2192stable; on **MCP overview**, client-green's server shifts to mcp-stable; flaky drains and its error ratio decays (half-open probing). |\n\n**Transitions to narrate:** entering *open* everything resets instantly (rules live in shared memory, applied per request). Leaving *protect-upstreams* the 429s stop the moment the limit series vanishes. Entering *full-control* reroutes ramp within ~2 s because green recycles sessions every 7 tool calls.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "Demo guide",
      "type": "text"
